1
00:00:01,500 --> 00:00:02,370
What is life?
生命是什么？

2
00:00:03,170 --> 00:00:07,550
Like most great questions, this one is easy to ask but difficult to answer.
和大多数重大问题一样，这个问题问起来容易，回答起来却很难。

3
00:00:08,350 --> 00:00:15,212
The reason is simple: we know of just one type of life and it’s challenging to do science with a sample size of one.
原因很简单：我们只知道一种生命，而在样本量只有一个的情况下做科学研究很有挑战性。

4
00:00:16,012 --> 00:00:23,472
The field of artificial life — called ALife for short — is the systematic attempt to spell out life’s fundamental principles.
人工生命（简称ALife）这一领域，是一种系统性的尝试，旨在阐明生命的基本原理。

5
00:00:24,272 --> 00:00:32,332
Many of its practitioners, so-called ALifers, think that somehow making life is the surest way to really understand what life is.
该领域的许多从业者，也就是所谓的ALifer（人工生命研究者），认为设法造出生命是真正理解生命为何物的最可靠途径。

6
00:00:33,132 --> 00:00:36,292
So far no one has convincingly made artificial life.
迄今为止，还没有人令人信服地造出人工生命。

7
00:00:37,092 --> 00:00:44,482
This track record makes ALife a ripe target for criticism, such as declarations of the field’s doubtful scientific value.
这样的过往记录使ALife成了现成的批评靶子，比如有人宣称这一领域的科学价值值得怀疑。

8
00:00:45,282 --> 00:00:49,732
Alan Smith, a complexity scientist, is tired of such complaints.
复杂性科学家艾伦·史密斯已经厌倦了这类抱怨。

9
00:00:50,532 --> 00:00:55,702
Asking about “the point” of ALife might be, well, missing the point entirely, he says.
他说，追问ALife有什么“意义”，或许，嗯，完全没抓住要点。

10
00:00:56,502 --> 00:01:01,012
“The existence of a living system is not about the use of anything,” Alan says.
“生命系统的存在与它有没有用无关，”艾伦说。

11
00:01:01,812 --> 00:01:05,402
“Some people ask me, ‘So what’s the worth of artificial life?’
“有人问我：‘那么，人工生命有什么价值呢？’

12
00:01:06,202 --> 00:01:09,252
Do you ever think, ‘What is the worth of your grandmother?’”
你会不会去想：‘你祖母有什么价值？’”

13
00:01:10,052 --> 00:01:18,322
As much as many ALifers hate emphasizing their research’s applications, the attempts to create artificial life could have practical payoffs.
尽管许多ALifer很不愿意强调自己研究的应用，但创造人工生命的尝试有可能带来实际的回报。

14
00:01:19,122 --> 00:01:27,992
Artificial intelligence may be considered ALife’s cousin in that researchers in both fields are enamored with a concept called open-ended evolution.
人工智能或许可以看作ALife的“表亲”，因为这两个领域的研究者都迷恋一个叫作“开放式演化”的概念。

15
00:01:28,792 --> 00:01:35,812
This is the capacity for a system to create essentially endless complexity, to be a sort of “novelty generator”.
这指的是一个系统创造出近乎无穷无尽的复杂性、成为某种“新奇事物生成器”的能力。

16
00:01:36,612 --> 00:01:39,792
The only system known to exhibit this is Earth’s biosphere.
已知唯一能表现出这种能力的系统是地球的生物圈。

17
00:01:40,592 --> 00:01:50,362
If the field of ALife manages to reproduce life’s endless “creativity” in some virtual model, those same principles could give rise to truly inventive machines.
如果ALife领域能够在某个虚拟模型中重现生命无穷无尽的“创造力”，那么同样的原理就可能催生出真正富有创造性的机器。

18
00:01:51,162 --> 00:01:56,042
Compared with developments in AI, advances in ALife are harder to recognize.
与人工智能的发展相比，ALife的进展更难辨识。

19
00:01:56,842 --> 00:02:03,082
One reason is that ALife is a field in which the central concept — life itself — is undefined.
原因之一在于，ALife这一领域的核心概念——生命本身——尚无定义。

20
00:02:03,882 --> 00:02:06,902
The lack of agreement among ALifers doesn’t help either.
ALifer之间缺乏共识，这也无济于事。

21
00:02:07,702 --> 00:02:12,672
The result is a diverse range of projects that each advance along their unique paths.
结果就是出现了各种各样的项目，每个项目都沿着自己独特的道路推进。

22
00:02:13,472 --> 00:02:17,392
For better or worse, ALife mirrors the very subject it studies.
不论是好是坏，ALife都恰恰映照出它所研究的对象本身。

23
00:02:18,192 --> 00:02:24,442
Its muddled progression is a striking parallel to the evolutionary struggles that have shaped Earth’s biosphere.
它混乱的发展历程，与生物演化中塑造了地球生物圈的种种艰难挣扎惊人地相似。

24
00:02:25,242 --> 00:02:31,662
Undefined and uncontrolled, ALife drives its followers to repurpose old ideas and generate novelty.
ALife既无定义，又不受控制，这驱使其追随者为旧观念找到新用途，并创造出新奇事物。

25
00:02:32,462 --> 00:02:38,332
It may be, of course, that these characteristics aren’t in any way surprising or singular.
当然，也可能这些特点丝毫不令人惊讶，也并非独一无二。

26
00:02:39,132 --> 00:02:42,192
They may apply universally to all acts of evolution.
它们可能普遍适用于一切演化活动。

27
00:02:42,992 --> 00:02:45,192
Ultimately ALife may be nothing special.
归根结底，ALife可能并没有什么特别之处。

28
00:02:45,992 --> 00:02:53,714
But even this dismissal suggests something: perhaps, just like life itself throughout the universe, the rise of ALife will prove unavoidable.
但即便是这种否定也说明了一点：或许，就像生命本身在整个宇宙中的兴起一样，ALife的兴起终将被证明是不可避免的。
